  "caption": "Loneliness isn’t always having nobody around.\n\nSometimes it’s having nobody around whom you can stop performing.\n\nCoaching: https://jasonleedaniel.com\n\n#Loneliness #HumanConnection #MentalHealth #JasonDaniel",
  "transcript": {
    "text": "Loneliness isn't just the absence of people. It's the absence of being known. That's why filling your calendar doesn't always fill the hole. You can be surrounded by friends, coworkers, even family, and still feel completely alone. Most people try to outrun loneliness with distraction. More scrolling, more noise, more entertainment, more people. But loneliness isn't asking for more stimulation. It's asking for more connection. And connection starts with you. Can you sit with yourself without immediately reaching for your phone? Can you become someone you enjoy spending time with? Because if you can't stand your own company, no amount of other people will permanently fix it. The odd thing is the less desperate you become to escape loneliness, the more capable you become of building real relationships. You're no longer looking for someone to rescue you. You're looking for someone to share the journey with. Loneliness isn't always a sign that something is wrong with your life. Sometimes it's an invitation to build one that's worth sharing. Hey, you made it this far. Hopefully, you can uh, check out my books. Uh, DM me for links. Thanks.",
